T*
() Tj
T*
(Session finish does not perform heavy Firebase work directly. It schedules a queued) Tj
T*
(upload.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Upload phases:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Session root/core.) Tj
T*
(2. Day metadata.) Tj
T*
(3. Day timeline.) Tj
T*
(4. Day summary.) Tj
T*
(5. Week summary.) Tj
T*
(6. Representative reps.) Tj
T*
(7. Set details.) Tj
T*
(8. Rep sets.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The firmware preserves final Firebase shape while splitting payloads when memory is) Tj
T*
(low.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Queue and Chunking Behavior) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The firmware uses memory modes:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Normal.) Tj
T*
(- Constrained.) Tj
T*
(- Critical.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(RepSet upload limits:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Normal: target 1900 bytes, hard max 2100 bytes, up to 6 reps per patch.) Tj
T*
(- Constrained: target 900 bytes, hard max 1100 bytes, up to 3 reps per patch.) Tj
T*
(- Critical: target 650 bytes, hard max 850 bytes, up to 2 reps per patch.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The final Firebase structure remains:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```text) Tj
T*
(repSets/set1/reps/0) Tj
T*
(repSets/set1/reps/1) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(No chunk nodes are added to the final schema.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
